<title>HONG KONG: HK money rates firmer, paper yields mixed.</title>
<headline>HK money rates firmer, paper yields mixed.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong interbank rates were firmer and government paper yields were mixed on Thursday in moderate trading, dealers said.</p>
<p>Overnight cash rose to 5-1/2 7/16 from 5-5/16 1/4 as strong demand on short-dated cash typical in the run-up to Chinese New Year tightened liquidity, one dealer said.</p>
<p>Three-month money was steady at 5-7/16 3/8.</p>
<p>Trading in government paper market was moderate.</p>
<p>One-week Exchange Fund bill yields edged up to 4.43 percent from 4.19 percent.</p>
</text>
